Phase24 opt-in change for the external `tools/elmer-hypre` source tree.

Apply the equivalent hunks to:
`src/fem/src/modules/HeatSolve.F90`

```diff
@@
   ! Default variable name
   CALL ListAddNewString( Params,'Variable','Temperature')
+
+  ! Phase24 is deliberately opt-in.  This selects the existing vectorized
+  ! CRS glue path for the legacy HeatSolve route without changing the
+  ! physical model or enabling timestep/matrix-value reuse.
+  CALL ListAddNewLogical( Params,'Phase24 Vector Assembly',.FALSE.)
@@
         TransientAssembly, Converged, AnyMultiply, NeedFlowSol
+     LOGICAL :: Phase24VectorAssembly
@@
     SolverParams => GetSolverParams()
+     Phase24VectorAssembly = GetLogical(SolverParams, 'Phase24 Vector Assembly', Found)
@@
-            CALL DefaultUpdateEquations( STIFF, FORCE )
+            CALL DefaultUpdateEquations( STIFF, FORCE, VecAssembly=Phase24VectorAssembly )
@@
-      CALL DefaultUpdateEquations( STIFF, FORCE )
+      CALL DefaultUpdateEquations( STIFF, FORCE, VecAssembly=Phase24VectorAssembly )
```

The working external source tree has this change applied. The default remains
`False`; enable it only in a dedicated comparison SIF:

```text
  Phase24 Vector Assembly = Logical True
```

This patch is intentionally limited to the existing vectorized CRS glue. It
does not enable matrix-value reuse, HYPRE/preconditioner reuse, or a new GPU
backend. A production default change requires the Phase24 regression gate and
same-case wall benchmark to pass first.

The cache implementation additionally records pointer identity for the CSR
`Rows` and `Cols` arrays. A same-sized reallocation therefore starts a fresh
destination cache instead of using positions from the previous CSR storage.
The opt-in flag is also checked at solver initialization: only a 3-D scalar
P1-tetra bulk mesh enters the Phase24 vector/cache path; unsupported cases
fall back to generic Elmer assembly automatically.

For eligible bodies, `HeatSolve.F90` also caches constant scalar `Heat Capacity`
and isotropic `Heat Conductivity` values by body id. If either property is
MATC/UDF, time-dependent, or anisotropic, that body is marked non-cacheable and
continues through `GetReal`/`ListGetRealArray` on the generic path.

The working source tree also has the opt-in wall markers enabled by:

```diff
@@
+  CALL ListAddNewLogical( Params,'Phase24 Wall Profiling',.FALSE.)
@@
+     LOGICAL :: Phase24WallProfiling
@@
+     Phase24WallProfiling = GetLogical(SolverParams, 'Phase24 Wall Profiling', Found)
```

With `Phase24 Wall Profiling = Logical True`, the legacy route emits REAL-time
measurements for UDF/circuit, bulk assembly, boundary assembly, matrix
finalization, and the linear solve. These are coarse first-stage measurements;
the bulk section must be split further before claiming a complete assembly
breakdown.
